WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:01.968
-President Trump

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:02.969
held a rally in Georgia,

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:03.969
where he defended

00:00:03.969 --> 00:00:05.305
his possibly illegal phone call

00:00:05.305 --> 00:00:06.973
pressuring Georgia
election officials

00:00:06.973 --> 00:00:08.674
to overturn his loss
to Joe Biden.

00:00:08.674 --> 00:00:10.977
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:14.847
♪♪

00:00:14.847 --> 00:00:17.317
On Monday night, Trump held
what will very likely be

00:00:17.317 --> 00:00:19.719
his last rally as president
of the United States

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:21.721
and, man,
it feels good to say that.

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:24.557
I feel like Tom Cruise jumping
on Oprah's couch.

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:27.260
You guys remember that, when
that was like a five-day story?

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:28.428
Now, things happen so fast that,

00:00:28.428 --> 00:00:30.630
when a celebrity jumps
off a couch cushion,

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.331
it's old news
by the time they land.

00:00:32.331 --> 00:00:34.701
And, look, I know Trump's going
to keep holding rallies

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:37.003
after he leaves office
because it's either that

00:00:37.003 --> 00:00:40.039
or pay for therapy,
but it just won't be the same.

00:00:40.039 --> 00:00:42.775
I mean, you can still go
to Grateful Dead concerts,

00:00:42.775 --> 00:00:44.410
but it's like two
of the original guys

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:45.645
and it ends at 9:30,

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:47.346
people are dancing
with knee braces on

00:00:47.346 --> 00:00:49.415
and, instead of joints,
they're passing around

00:00:49.415 --> 00:00:50.616
a tube of Fixodent.

00:00:50.616 --> 00:00:52.251
As president, Trump has power

00:00:52.251 --> 00:00:53.519
and we have to listen to him.

00:00:53.519 --> 00:00:56.088
But, in two weeks, he'll just be
a guy hosting a show

00:00:56.088 --> 00:00:58.824
from whatever rental van
they shoot Newsmax out of,

00:00:58.824 --> 00:01:00.860
ranting about low-flush toilets

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:02.628
and B-list celebrities
from the '90s.

00:01:02.628 --> 00:01:04.831
[ As Trump ]
Bobby Knight -- "The General,"
they called him.

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:07.100
Met him at an after-party
for the ESPYs, 1994.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:08.968
Nasty guy.
Mean guy.

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:10.102
Nice to me, though.

00:01:10.102 --> 00:01:11.470
Remember when he threw
that chair?

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:13.272
Real son of a bitch.

00:01:13.272 --> 00:01:16.342
One time, I saw him
stab a waiter with a fork.

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:18.044
Charity benefit.
Donated nothing.

00:01:18.044 --> 00:01:19.679
Ate the food and left.
Real piece of [bleep]

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:23.449
[ Laughter ]
Liked me. Liked me.

00:01:23.449 --> 00:01:25.618
If there's one takeaway
from the Trump presidency,

00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:29.656
let it be that --
the man loved a rally.

00:01:29.656 --> 00:01:31.290
Remember, he even started
his phone call

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:33.459
with Georgia Secretary of State
Brad Raffensperger

00:01:33.459 --> 00:01:36.496
by claiming there's no way
he could've lost the election

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:37.964
because of the size
of his rallies.

00:02:08.528 --> 00:02:11.264
Okay, first of all, Biden had
small numbers of people

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:13.866
because it's a [bleep] pandemic,
you sociopath.

00:02:13.866 --> 00:02:16.135
Luring people
into tightly packed crowds

00:02:16.135 --> 00:02:17.236
for hours at a time,

00:02:17.236 --> 00:02:19.038
with a highly contagious
and deadly disease

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:20.739
spreading rapidly
through the air

00:02:20.739 --> 00:02:22.442
is like something
the Joker would do.

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:23.643
Although, knowing the Joker,

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:25.745
he'd probably add some
unnecessary logistics,

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:28.114
where there are like two rallies
happening simultaneously

00:02:28.114 --> 00:02:30.016
and one has a bomb
and the other has poison gas.

00:02:30.016 --> 00:02:31.917
Batman's girlfriend's at one
and Alfred's at the other.

00:02:31.917 --> 00:02:33.018
And, meanwhile,
Batman's thinking,

00:02:33.018 --> 00:02:34.687
"I can't wait until Gotham City

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:36.388
is rid of this insufferable
ass[bleep],"

00:02:36.388 --> 00:02:38.257
not knowing, of course,
that the villain after the Joker

00:02:38.257 --> 00:02:40.159
[ As Bane ]
is going to sound like this!

00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:41.427
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:42.862
So much for my
New Year's resolution

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:44.497
not to lean
on the Bane impression.

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:47.567
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:50.970
Also, the reason Biden
didn't need big rallies is

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:53.639
because people
weren't voting for him,

00:02:53.639 --> 00:02:55.541
they were voting against you.

00:02:55.541 --> 00:02:57.710
One of the reasons they were
voting against you is

00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:00.346
because of the way
you behaved at rallies.

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:03.415
So the irony is
Biden did have giant rallies.

00:03:03.415 --> 00:03:04.951
They were just yours.

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:06.753
And you have to love
that big crowds

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:08.687
was Trump's first argument
right out of the gate.

00:03:08.687 --> 00:03:11.390
I'm surprised he didn't
follow up with hard evidence

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:12.925
of "Most red hats sold"

00:03:12.925 --> 00:03:15.527
or "Candidate whose name
Jeanine Pirro says the loudest."

00:03:15.527 --> 00:03:17.430
And Trump should've been
ready for this call.

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:18.565
According
to The Washington Post...

00:03:29.575 --> 00:03:33.146
And prank call is a perfectly
reasonable thing to think.

00:03:33.146 --> 00:03:35.347
If you read the transcript
of Trump's phone call

00:03:35.347 --> 00:03:37.249
with Raffensperger
and his lawyer Ryan Germany

00:03:37.249 --> 00:03:38.851
in a different voice,

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:41.020
you'd think it was one
of the Jerky Boys.

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:42.622 line:0%
[ As Jerky Boy ]

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:55.935 line:0%
[ As Jerky Boy ]

00:04:00.039 --> 00:04:01.874 line:0%
[ As Jerky Boy ]

00:04:04.477 --> 00:04:06.713
They were a cultural phenomenon.

00:04:06.713 --> 00:04:08.047
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.047 --> 00:04:12.051
If you were a young man in 1993,

00:04:12.051 --> 00:04:15.921
the Jerky Boys were loud
and the parties were hopping.

00:04:15.921 --> 00:04:17.089
So Trump thinks rally size

00:04:17.089 --> 00:04:18.524
is proof he actually
won the election.

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:20.893
Well, Monday night
gave him one last chance

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:23.463
to show off
that oratorical prowess

00:04:23.463 --> 00:04:26.365
he's so legendary for,
and he did not disappoint.

00:04:26.365 --> 00:04:30.269
-We have made Ame...rica
strong again.

00:04:30.269 --> 00:04:32.504
[ Cheering ]
Look at that arm.
Look at that.

00:04:32.504 --> 00:04:35.307
-While it's troubling
that someone who runs America

00:04:35.307 --> 00:04:36.743
can't say "America,"

00:04:36.743 --> 00:04:40.078
[ Laughing ]
"Look at that arm"
is a terrific save.

00:04:40.078 --> 00:04:41.447
Did he say "Amurrica"?

00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:43.816
"Shhh!
I'm looking at his arm!"

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:45.584
And, hey, anyone's capable
of making a mistake,

00:04:45.584 --> 00:04:47.086
but you never hear
Angela Merkel say --

00:04:47.086 --> 00:04:48.654
[ As Merkel ]
We love our country,

00:04:48.654 --> 00:04:50.256
Juzmuhkey.

00:04:50.256 --> 00:04:52.191
[ Laughter ]
Look at the haircut!

00:04:52.191 --> 00:04:55.561
[ Laughter ]

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:57.096
This is what happens
when you zap your brain

00:04:57.096 --> 00:04:58.931
with 20 hours
of cable news a day.

00:04:58.931 --> 00:05:00.966
Your aides have to pump you full
of Red Bull and Adderall

00:05:00.966 --> 00:05:03.102
just to get you through a speech
and, by the end of it,

00:05:03.102 --> 00:05:06.171
your primary motor cortex starts
to turn into cottage cheese.

00:05:06.171 --> 00:05:09.809
I mean, compare his frantic,
slurring energy during the rally

00:05:09.809 --> 00:05:11.844
with this photo
his daughter Ivanka posted

00:05:11.844 --> 00:05:14.680
on the plane
on the way to the rally.

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:16.048
[ Laughs ]

00:05:16.048 --> 00:05:17.382
There's that quality

00:05:17.382 --> 00:05:19.852
father-daughter time
every family dreams about.

00:05:19.852 --> 00:05:21.521
"Dad, I want to take a picture."

00:05:21.521 --> 00:05:22.989
[ As Trump ]
Then take it!

00:05:22.989 --> 00:05:24.223
[ Laughter ]

00:05:24.223 --> 00:05:25.257
It looks like the photo you see

00:05:25.257 --> 00:05:26.559
when you see a retired athlete

00:05:26.559 --> 00:05:28.361
at your airport gate
and don't want to bother them.

00:05:28.361 --> 00:05:30.796
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.796 --> 00:05:32.865
Trump was supposedly there
to rally votes

00:05:32.865 --> 00:05:35.401
for GOP Senate candidates
Kelly Loeffler and David Perdue,

00:05:35.401 --> 00:05:38.237
two of the most soulless,
vacant, D.C. robots

00:05:38.237 --> 00:05:39.405
you'll ever see in politics.

00:05:39.405 --> 00:05:40.873
As far as I can tell, neither

00:05:40.873 --> 00:05:43.042
has any discernible
policy positions,

00:05:43.042 --> 00:05:44.877
other than wanting to be
a senator and making money.

00:05:44.877 --> 00:05:47.512
For example, here's Loeffler,
a Wall Street executive

00:05:47.512 --> 00:05:49.348
who's originally from Illinois,
trying to sound like

00:05:49.348 --> 00:05:51.083
a character
in a Tennessee Williams play.

00:05:51.083 --> 00:05:52.551
-Let's give the senator a hand.

00:05:52.551 --> 00:05:54.487
-Whoo! [ Applause ]
He has worked
so hard for y'all.

00:05:54.487 --> 00:05:55.688
And y'all are working hard.

00:05:55.688 --> 00:05:58.156
I have a very important
question for y'all.

00:05:58.156 --> 00:06:00.292
Grateful for y'all.
That's why y'all are here.

00:06:00.292 --> 00:06:02.261
We need y'all
to get out and vote.

00:06:02.261 --> 00:06:04.463
-It's like watching someone
audition for Tami Taylor

00:06:04.463 --> 00:06:06.699
in a dinner theater production
of "Friday Night Lights."

00:06:06.699 --> 00:06:08.601
"Okay, Kelly, can you maybe
do it one more time,

00:06:08.601 --> 00:06:10.203
but, this time,
don't say 'y'all' so much?"

00:06:10.203 --> 00:06:11.937
[ As Loeffler ]
Y'all got it, y'all.

00:06:11.937 --> 00:06:13.005
Trump was supposed to be there

00:06:13.005 --> 00:06:15.107
to campaign
for Loeffler and Perdue,

00:06:15.107 --> 00:06:18.344
so, naturally, he started out
by immediately obsessing

00:06:18.344 --> 00:06:19.679
over his election loss.

00:06:19.679 --> 00:06:20.946
[ Cheering ]
-Hello, Georgia. By the way...

00:06:20.946 --> 00:06:22.748
-[ Screaming ]
-...there's no way

00:06:22.748 --> 00:06:24.684
we lost Georgia.
There's no way.

00:06:24.684 --> 00:06:27.687
-That has to be the fastest use
of "by the way"

00:06:27.687 --> 00:06:30.589
in any speech, ever.
You weren't even on the way yet.

00:06:30.589 --> 00:06:32.257
Give yourself some runway,
buddy.

00:06:32.257 --> 00:06:33.893
If you wake up next
to your spouse

00:06:33.893 --> 00:06:35.661
and say, "Good morning.
By the way,"

00:06:35.661 --> 00:06:38.965
they're going to know you were
lying awake, furious all night.

00:06:38.965 --> 00:06:40.499
Trump tried to talk
about the Senate race,

00:06:40.499 --> 00:06:41.834
but every time he mentioned it,
he couldn't help

00:06:41.834 --> 00:06:44.570
but veer back
into nursing his wounded ego.

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:46.705
-If the liberal Democrats
take the Senate

00:06:46.705 --> 00:06:48.141
or the White House --

00:06:48.141 --> 00:06:49.541
And they're not taking
this White House.

00:06:49.541 --> 00:06:50.776
We're going to fight like hell.

00:06:50.776 --> 00:06:52.578
I'll tell you right now.
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:06:52.578 --> 00:06:58.484
These Senate seats are truly
the last line of defense.

00:06:58.484 --> 00:07:00.319
Now, I must preface that
by saying --

00:07:00.319 --> 00:07:03.089
because they'll say,
"He just conceded!"

00:07:03.089 --> 00:07:05.791
[ Booing ]
No, no, I don't think so.

00:07:05.791 --> 00:07:07.793
-There's nothing to concede.
It's over.

00:07:07.793 --> 00:07:09.895
It doesn't matter
whether you concede or not.

00:07:09.895 --> 00:07:11.564
I mean, you can try it,
just to see how it feels,

00:07:11.564 --> 00:07:13.599
see if your first moment
of self-reflection

00:07:13.599 --> 00:07:15.434
and acceptance of failure
in 74 years

00:07:15.434 --> 00:07:16.969
has a Grinch-like effect

00:07:16.969 --> 00:07:18.737
of growing your heart
three sizes,

00:07:18.737 --> 00:07:21.940
at which point it will be as big
as what the Grinch started with.

00:07:21.940 --> 00:07:24.243
And yet,
even after Trump's corrupt

00:07:24.243 --> 00:07:27.613
and possibly illegal phone call,
Republicans are still going

00:07:27.613 --> 00:07:30.016
along with his attempt
to subvert the election

00:07:30.016 --> 00:07:31.483
for the sake of their own
political interests.

00:07:31.483 --> 00:07:33.786
During the rally,
Loeffler jumped up to the mic

00:07:33.786 --> 00:07:35.854
to tell the crowd
she'd be objecting

00:07:35.854 --> 00:07:37.222
to the Electoral College vote

00:07:37.222 --> 00:07:39.725
and implied
that it would somehow work.

00:07:39.725 --> 00:07:41.494
-Hello, Georgia!

00:07:41.494 --> 00:07:43.329
Whoo!

00:07:43.329 --> 00:07:45.331
[ Cheering and applause ]
Thank you, Georgia!

00:07:45.331 --> 00:07:48.367
I have an announcement, Georgia.

00:07:48.367 --> 00:07:50.002
On January 6th,

00:07:50.002 --> 00:07:53.371
I will object
to the Electoral College vote.

00:07:53.371 --> 00:07:54.573
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:07:54.573 --> 00:07:56.742
That's right.

00:07:56.742 --> 00:07:57.776
That's right.

00:07:57.776 --> 00:07:58.777
Thank you.

00:07:58.777 --> 00:07:59.778
[ Whistling ]

00:07:59.778 --> 00:08:01.647
We're going to get this done!

00:08:01.647 --> 00:08:03.015
Alright, Georgia!

00:08:03.015 --> 00:08:05.751
But I have a very important
question for you.

00:08:05.751 --> 00:08:09.722
Are you ready to show America
that Georgia's a red state?

00:08:09.722 --> 00:08:11.791
-Yeah!

00:08:11.791 --> 00:08:13.358
-She can't overturn
the election results,

00:08:13.358 --> 00:08:15.961
but she did overturn
her own Southern accent.

00:08:15.961 --> 00:08:18.130
I mean, where did it go?
Did Antifa steal it?

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:20.132
She could've at least
thrown a "y'all" in there.

00:08:20.132 --> 00:08:22.534
She didn't even say,
"Get this done"

00:08:22.534 --> 00:08:23.603
in a Southern accent.

00:08:23.603 --> 00:08:25.437
She sounds like
Larry the Cable Guy

00:08:25.437 --> 00:08:27.106
after elocution lessons.

00:08:27.106 --> 00:08:28.707
[ Southern accent ]
It's like we say down here
in the South --

00:08:28.707 --> 00:08:29.942
[ posh accent ]
Get her done.

00:08:29.942 --> 00:08:31.243
[ Laughter ]

00:08:31.243 --> 00:08:33.345
Of course, what she's describing
is not possible,

00:08:33.345 --> 00:08:35.647
legal, or constitutional.
It was already sedition

00:08:35.647 --> 00:08:37.416
when Republicans
were attempting to overturn

00:08:37.416 --> 00:08:39.452
a free and fair election
before Trump's call,

00:08:39.452 --> 00:08:41.453
but to get onboard
after the call

00:08:41.453 --> 00:08:43.222
is just shocking
in its brazenness.

00:08:43.222 --> 00:08:45.591
I mean, the guy may have
committed a crime

00:08:45.591 --> 00:08:47.860
by basically admitting he was
trying to steal the election

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:49.662
and Republicans are like,
"Sign me up."

00:08:49.662 --> 00:08:50.930
They're shoving it in our faces.

00:08:50.930 --> 00:08:52.731
They're like suspects
in a police lineup,

00:08:52.731 --> 00:08:55.267
raising their hands, saying,
"It was me! I did it!

00:08:55.267 --> 00:08:57.202
Can I go now?
I can? Good.

00:08:57.202 --> 00:08:58.704
To jail?!"

00:08:58.704 --> 00:09:00.739
You can't pretend this is about
high-minded principle anymore.

00:09:00.739 --> 00:09:01.974
After that phone call,
it's clear

00:09:01.974 --> 00:09:04.142
what this is really about --
stealing votes

00:09:04.142 --> 00:09:06.645
to assuage Trump's ego
and illegally cling to power.

00:09:06.645 --> 00:09:09.214
And, even after the phone call
came out, Trump is, of course,

00:09:09.214 --> 00:09:11.250
still insisting there was
nothing wrong with it.

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:12.551
-They talked
about my phone call.

00:09:12.551 --> 00:09:13.552
They don't like my phone call.

00:09:13.552 --> 00:09:15.087
Everyone
loved my phone call.

00:09:15.087 --> 00:09:16.622
-My God, he sounds like
a Hollywood director

00:09:16.622 --> 00:09:18.591
talking himself up
after a big flop.

00:09:18.591 --> 00:09:20.559
"Everyone love my movie.
They said they prefer

00:09:20.559 --> 00:09:22.728
the version with the
unblurred buttholes."

00:09:22.728 --> 00:09:24.563
No, no one loved your call.

00:09:24.563 --> 00:09:27.199
Even Republicans who are
diehard Trump loyalists

00:09:27.199 --> 00:09:28.433
and who have signed on
to the attempt

00:09:28.433 --> 00:09:30.036
to reject
the Electoral College vote,

00:09:30.036 --> 00:09:32.337
like Tennessee
Senator Marsha Blackburn,

00:09:32.337 --> 00:09:35.440
gently tried to tiptoe
away from the phone call.

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:37.543
-Brian, one of the things

00:09:37.543 --> 00:09:39.545
I think that everyone has said

00:09:39.545 --> 00:09:45.817 line:0%
is that this call
was not a helpful call.

00:09:45.817 --> 00:09:48.554
-Oh, I'm so sorry the president
wasn't helpful to your attempt

00:09:48.554 --> 00:09:50.389
to steal the election
by blurting out

00:09:50.389 --> 00:09:51.957
what you were really trying
to do the whole time.

00:09:51.957 --> 00:09:54.259
Republicans all think
they're slick members

00:09:54.259 --> 00:09:55.694
of an elite heist squad trying

00:09:55.694 --> 00:09:57.829
to rob a precious jewel
from a museum,

00:09:57.829 --> 00:10:00.065
rappelling down into the vault
on a rope,

00:10:00.065 --> 00:10:02.334
jumping around lasers,
and Trump's the guy who just

00:10:02.334 --> 00:10:04.636
walks up to the security guard
with a hammer and says --

00:10:04.636 --> 00:10:06.572
[ As Trump ]
I'm here to steal
the fancy diamond.

00:10:06.572 --> 00:10:08.073
Oh, thank you, a map.
Excuse me.

00:10:08.073 --> 00:10:10.475
How does this map know
I am here?

00:10:10.475 --> 00:10:11.777
Does it move when I move?

00:10:11.777 --> 00:10:13.545
And, by the way,
just to be clear,

00:10:13.545 --> 00:10:15.180
the call may very well
have been illegal.

00:10:15.180 --> 00:10:17.649
The Georgia secretary of state
said there might be

00:10:17.649 --> 00:10:19.952
an investigation of the call,
and election law experts

00:10:19.952 --> 00:10:23.155
have said it seems like
it may be a crime.

00:10:23.155 --> 00:10:26.859
-Well, it sure sounds like what
the president was asking for was

00:10:26.859 --> 00:10:29.495 line:0%
for the secretary of state
to manufacture votes,

00:10:29.495 --> 00:10:32.464 line:0%
just enough votes to give him
a one-vote margin in Georgia.

00:10:32.464 --> 00:10:33.866 line:0%
It's not clear
how this would work.

00:10:33.866 --> 00:10:36.001 line:0%
George's already sent in
its Electoral College votes,

00:10:36.001 --> 00:10:39.705 line:0%
but it sounds like it could be
a crime under both federal law

00:10:39.705 --> 00:10:41.607 line:0%
and under state law,

00:10:41.607 --> 00:10:45.110 line:0%
because, when you ask someone
to come up with fake votes,

00:10:45.110 --> 00:10:47.646 line:0%
that's kind of the definition
of election fraud.

00:10:47.646 --> 00:10:49.615
-Yeah, of course it is.
If you try to fraudulently

00:10:49.615 --> 00:10:51.717
overturn an election,
that's election fraud.

00:10:51.717 --> 00:10:53.953
Seems pretty clear-cut to me,
but then again...

00:10:53.953 --> 00:10:55.888
[ Southern accent ]
I'm just a simple
country lawyer,

00:10:55.888 --> 00:10:59.458
like Kelly Loeffler, you all.

00:10:59.458 --> 00:11:01.793
[ Laughter ]

00:11:01.793 --> 00:11:03.462
You're from here
and you're from here!

00:11:03.462 --> 00:11:05.664
I'm not!
[ Laughter ]

00:11:05.664 --> 00:11:07.566
Trump tried to pressure
Georgia election officials

00:11:07.566 --> 00:11:09.168
and it didn't work,
so, now, he's trying to pressure

00:11:09.168 --> 00:11:10.602
his own vice president,
Mike Pence.

00:11:10.602 --> 00:11:12.238
Pence will have to preside
over the counting

00:11:12.238 --> 00:11:14.607
of electoral votes tomorrow.
Now, to be clear,

00:11:14.607 --> 00:11:17.342
Pence has no power
to just overturn the results,

00:11:17.342 --> 00:11:20.146
despite Trump's insistence
on Twitter today that...

00:11:23.715 --> 00:11:24.817
No, he doesn't.

00:11:24.817 --> 00:11:27.086
All Pence is supposed
to do is count.

00:11:27.086 --> 00:11:29.422
Pence can't change the results,
any more than Vanna White

00:11:29.422 --> 00:11:31.290
can change the phrase
on the board,

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:33.925
although, apparently, even
counting is difficult for Pence.

00:11:33.925 --> 00:11:34.994
The New York Times
reported that...

00:11:45.637 --> 00:11:47.439
...which is like me saying
it's gut-wrenching,

00:11:47.439 --> 00:11:49.741
balancing my years
preaching a healthy diet

00:11:49.741 --> 00:11:52.511
with my four-year-old's desire
to eat a thousand gummy worms.

00:11:52.511 --> 00:11:55.013
But spare a thought
for Mike Pence's gut

00:11:55.013 --> 00:11:56.615
because it's really been
through the wringer

00:11:56.615 --> 00:11:58.217
these past few years and, now,

00:11:58.217 --> 00:12:00.252
he has to choose
between the Constitution

00:12:00.252 --> 00:12:03.355
and a sleazy Mafia don
cold-calling election officials,

00:12:03.355 --> 00:12:05.824
illegally begging for votes
like a telemarketer.

00:12:05.824 --> 00:12:07.593
[ As Trump ]
Hello, this is the secretary
of state for Georgia?

00:12:07.593 --> 00:12:10.462
Are you happy
with your Internet service?

00:12:10.462 --> 00:12:13.632
Oh, what if I told you you could
combine Wi-Fi and cable

00:12:13.632 --> 00:12:16.735
for the price
of only 11,000 votes?

00:12:16.735 --> 00:12:18.136
And then, yesterday,
Trump added to the pressure

00:12:18.136 --> 00:12:19.838
by telling the crowd
he'd be mad at Pence

00:12:19.838 --> 00:12:22.707
if the vice president didn't
steal the election for him.

00:12:22.707 --> 00:12:25.277
-I hope Mike Pence
comes through for us.

00:12:25.277 --> 00:12:26.945
I have to tell you.
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:12:26.945 --> 00:12:31.149
I hope that our great
vice president,

00:12:31.149 --> 00:12:33.785
our great vice president,
comes through for us.

00:12:33.785 --> 00:12:36.021
He's a great guy.

00:12:36.021 --> 00:12:37.989
Of course,
if he doesn't come through,

00:12:37.989 --> 00:12:39.959
I won't like him quite as much.

00:12:39.959 --> 00:12:42.561
-I have a hard time believing
Trump likes Pence, even now.

00:12:42.561 --> 00:12:44.930
There's no way those two
have anything in common,

00:12:44.930 --> 00:12:46.765
aside from their
desperate desire

00:12:46.765 --> 00:12:48.367
to wield power at any cost.

00:12:48.367 --> 00:12:50.702
Trump gets what he needs
from Pence, and vice versa.

00:12:50.702 --> 00:12:52.271
They're like a rhino

00:12:52.271 --> 00:12:54.473
and that weird bird
that eats bugs off of them.

00:12:54.473 --> 00:12:56.107
If it weren't for the bugs,
they're not hanging out.

00:12:56.107 --> 00:12:57.776
By the way,
you can decide for yourself

00:12:57.776 --> 00:12:59.044
which is which.
I don't care.

00:12:59.044 --> 00:13:00.779
From the very beginning,
they've looked like

00:13:00.779 --> 00:13:02.147
two cops thrown together

00:13:02.147 --> 00:13:04.249
and forced to put aside
their differences to stop --

00:13:04.249 --> 00:13:06.217
or, in this case, start --
a crime spree.

00:13:06.217 --> 00:13:09.455
I think I saw it
last night on TNT.

00:13:09.455 --> 00:13:11.657
"Officer Ham, Officer Milk,
get in here!"

00:13:11.657 --> 00:13:12.791
[ Laughter ]

00:13:12.791 --> 00:13:13.825
[ As Trump ]
Milk, you've got to tell him

00:13:13.825 --> 00:13:16.294
you're the one
who crashed the cruiser.

00:13:16.294 --> 00:13:17.663
[ As Pence ]
It was you that
crashed the cruiser.

00:13:17.663 --> 00:13:18.964
[ As Trump ]
I didn't know it was
a one-way street!

00:13:18.964 --> 00:13:20.098
[ As Pence ]
It said one-way!

00:13:20.098 --> 00:13:21.567
[ As Trump ]
But it didn't say which way.

00:13:21.567 --> 00:13:23.469
[ Laughter ]
[ As Pence ] That's what
the arrow was for!

00:13:23.469 --> 00:13:26.271
[ As Trump ]
Who has time
to look at the arrow?!

00:13:26.271 --> 00:13:27.672
Plus, I was chasing a suspect.

00:13:27.672 --> 00:13:28.807
[ As Pence ]
You were trying
to get to McDonald's

00:13:28.807 --> 00:13:30.142
before they stopped
serving breakfast.

00:13:30.142 --> 00:13:31.877
[ As Trump ]
[ Laughs ] That's true.

00:13:31.877 --> 00:13:34.613
[ Laughter ]
You caught me in a fib.

00:13:34.613 --> 00:13:37.516
Oh, Milk.

00:13:37.516 --> 00:13:39.451
If I was a lady cop,

00:13:39.451 --> 00:13:41.887
would your wife have to be
in the car with us?
[ Laughter ]

00:13:41.887 --> 00:13:44.723
♪♪

00:13:44.723 --> 00:13:46.591
So tomorrow Congress
will count the votes

00:13:46.591 --> 00:13:48.560
that have already been cast
by the Electoral College.

00:13:48.560 --> 00:13:51.162
Again, Congress does not have
any authority to just overturn

00:13:51.162 --> 00:13:53.465
the results of a presidential
election and pick someone else.

00:13:53.465 --> 00:13:55.600
It's not a thing.
This isn't "American Idol."

00:13:55.600 --> 00:13:57.135
It's not like there's
an audience vote

00:13:57.135 --> 00:13:58.437
and then, Lionel Richie gets
to weigh in.

00:13:58.437 --> 00:14:00.672
Ted Cruz doesn't get a veto.

00:14:00.672 --> 00:14:02.273
Nowhere in the Constitution
does it say,

00:14:02.273 --> 00:14:04.943
"The president shall be chosen
by the Electoral College,

00:14:04.943 --> 00:14:09.547
unless a time-traveling
Old West bartender disagrees."

00:14:09.547 --> 00:14:11.149
[ As Cruz ]
I declare President Trump
the winner

00:14:11.149 --> 00:14:13.852
and sarsaparilla on the house!

00:14:13.852 --> 00:14:15.487
Republicans are running a scam

00:14:15.487 --> 00:14:17.122
by telling their voters
there's actually a chance

00:14:17.122 --> 00:14:19.491
objecting to tomorrow's
Electoral College certification

00:14:19.491 --> 00:14:22.060
will somehow allow Trump
to stay in office.

00:14:22.060 --> 00:14:24.530
Their entire case falls apart,
once you ask them for even

00:14:24.530 --> 00:14:26.831
the simplest explanation
of how this is supposed to work,

00:14:26.831 --> 00:14:29.735
and that's because it's all
a lie to conceal the truth,

00:14:29.735 --> 00:14:32.037
the truth Trump revealed
on his phone call.

00:14:32.037 --> 00:14:34.539
It's not about principle
or election integrity.

00:14:34.539 --> 00:14:35.808
It's about power.

00:14:35.808 --> 00:14:37.743
These guys believe their
opponents are illegitimate.

00:14:37.743 --> 00:14:39.211
They want to dismantle
our democracy

00:14:39.211 --> 00:14:41.213
and replace it
with an authoritarian state

00:14:41.213 --> 00:14:42.981
in which they're the only ones
who get to govern...

00:14:42.981 --> 00:14:45.150
-Ame...rica.

00:14:45.150 --> 00:14:47.820
[ Laughter ]
-This has been --
Look at my arm! --

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:48.854
"A Closer Look."

00:14:48.854 --> 00:14:52.424
♪♪

00:14:52.424 --> 00:14:54.259
God's Love We Deliver
cooks and brings

00:14:54.259 --> 00:14:55.594
over two million meals a year

00:14:55.594 --> 00:14:57.929
to men, women, and children
living with HIV/AIDS,

00:14:57.929 --> 00:14:59.764
cancer, and other
serious illness

00:14:59.764 --> 00:15:01.833
and they need your help,
now, more than ever.

00:15:01.833 --> 00:15:04.169
If you're watching this online,
you can hit the Donate button.

00:15:04.169 --> 00:15:06.371
Stay safe.
Wash your hands.

00:15:06.371 --> 00:15:08.374
Wear a mask.
We love you.

